# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, behaviour depends on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, which
# produces two problems: whole files showing as changed in a diff for no reason, and —
# far worse — binary assets being corrupted by line-ending conversion.

# Normalise text to LF in the repository, whatever the platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted. The sample PDFs are generated with a minimal
# writer whose cross-reference table stores byte offsets, so a single CRLF substitution
# shifts every offset and the file stops opening.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.whl   binary
*.gz    binary

# PowerShell and batch files are read by Windows tooling that expects CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
